,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Shatt,Nilo-Saharan
1,Sub-Saharan African music traditions - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-Saharan_African_music_traditions,"There are two broad categories of traditional Hausa music; rural folk music and urban court music developed in the Hausa Kingdoms before the Fulani War. Their folk music has played an important part in Nigerian music, contributing elements such as the goje, a one-stringed fiddle.",Shatt,Nilo-Saharan
2,Sahara Strings | Saharan Music – The Soul of the Desert.Saharan songs and music - YouTubeSub-Saharan African music traditions - WikipediaNilo-Saharan languages - WikipediaMusic from Saharan WhatsApp - Sahel Sounds CompilationsTop Shatta Songs - ChosicShatt – Apple Music,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_LhAfJZ7NZU,"Aug 17, 2025 · Authentic Saharan music blending Tuareg rhythms, desert guitar, and timeless nomadic spirit. A journey through golden dunes, mystical nights, and melodies that heal the soul. 🎶 May 25, 2025 · 🎼🎸Saharan Songs and Music A musical journey through the desert: hypnotic rhythms, Tuareg guitars, ancestral chants, and nomadic poetry. There are two broad categories of traditional Hausa music; rural folk music and urban court music developed in the Hausa Kingdoms before the Fulani War. Their folk music has played an important part in Nigerian music, contributing elements such as the goje, a one-stringed fiddle. As indicated by its hyphenated name, Nilo-Saharan is a family of the African interior, including the greater Nile Basin and the Central Sahara Desert. Most of its proposed constituent divisions are found in the modern countries of Sudan and South Sudan, through which the Nile River flows. This series consisted of ephemeral digital EPs, documenting live performances by some of the most exciting acts in the Sahel playing music, including Nigerién techno, wedding rock, Woodabe guitar, WZN, traditional music, Mandingue music, and more. Top shatta tracks right now, ranked by relevance to this genre and popularity on Spotify. Écoutez la musique de Shatt sur Apple Music. Découvrez les morceaux et albums les plus écoutés de Shatt, notamment SIN REGRESO (feat. SHATT) et Conscious Reality.",Shatt,Nilo-Saharan
